-- title:
--   Halving a lift of an endomorphism at a place above 2
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ has characteristic $2$, and let $W$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$. Let $\alpha_0$ be an additive endomorphism of the group of affine points $W(\kappa)$ lying in `rationalHomSet`, i.e. either $\alpha_0 = 0$ or there are bivariate polynomials $n_X, d_X, n_Y, d_Y$ over $\kappa$ and a finite set $B \subseteq \kappa$ such that on every nonsingular point $(x,y)$ with $x \notin B$ the denominators do not vanish and $\alpha_0(x,y) = (n_X/d_X, n_Y/d_Y)$ evaluated at $(x,y)$. Let $t, q \in \mathbb{Z}$ satisfy $\alpha_0 \circ \alpha_0 + q\cdot\mathrm{id} = t\cdot\alpha_0$, with $m^2 - tm + q \neq 0$ for every integer $m$, $t$ odd and $q$ even. Assume that $2\alpha_0$ lifts to $A$: there are a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $A$ whose reduction $E \bmod \mathfrak{m}_A$ has nonzero discriminant, a variable change $v$ over $\kappa$ with $v \cdot (E \bmod \mathfrak{m}_A) = W$, and an element $\gamma$ of `rationalHomSet` for $E \otimes_A \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (rationally represented in the same sense over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, or zero), such that for every point $P$ of $E$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the reduction of $\gamma(P)$, transported to $W(\kappa)$ by the point bijection attached to $v$, equals $(2\cdot\alpha_0)$ applied to the likewise transported reduction of $P$; here reduction sends a point with integral $x$-coordinate to the residues of its coordinates and a point with non-integral $x$-coordinate to the origin. The conclusion asserts the same data with $\alpha_0$ in place of $2\alpha_0$: there exist a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $A$ with reduction of nonzero discriminant, a variable change $v$ over $\kappa$ with $v \cdot (E \bmod \mathfrak{m}_A) = W$, and $\alpha$ in `rationalHomSet` for $E \otimes_A \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, whose reduction, transported by $v$, agrees with $\alpha_0$ on all of $W(\kappa)$.
--
--   This is the case of Deuring's lifting theorem at the residue characteristic $2$ in which $2$ splits in the imaginary quadratic order generated by $\alpha_0$ (trace odd, norm even), where the endomorphism itself, rather than its double, must be lifted to characteristic zero at the given place. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_comp_reduceHom_of_comp_self_add_smul_eq_smul`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_comp_reduceHom_of_comp_self_add_smul_eq_smul), which assembles the lifting statement for an arbitrary endomorphism satisfying an irreducible quadratic relation.
